 this album featured liner notes written by Marvin Gaye himself, which included a quote from T.S. Eliot: \"birth and copulation and death.\" While undoubtedly about sex, the album is also described as being as \"socially and politically aware\" as his earlier \"What's Going On.\" Sociology professor Michael Eric Dyson praised it as a brave album for a black man to create such erotic content, directly countering the black exploitation films of the era by celebrating black sexuality, eroticism, and love. It reflects a part of the sexual revolution that viewed sexual freedom as beautiful, natural, and potentially a \"gift from God.\" \"Marvin Gaye released the Let's Get An On album in 1973.\"","year":1973,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 4 - Music of the 70s (Sexual) Revolution","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/ep-4-talkin-bout-a-sexual-revolution"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Erotic and Socially Aware","body":"Released in 1973, this album featured liner notes written by Marvin Gaye himself, which included a quote from T.S. Eliot: \"birth and copulation and death.\" While undoubtedly about sex, the album is also described as being as \"socially and politically aware\" as his earlier \"What's Going On.\" Sociology professor Michael Eric Dyson praised it as a brave album for a black man to create such erotic content, directly countering the black exploitation films of the era by celebrating black sexuality, eroticism, and love. It reflects a part of the sexual revolution that viewed sexual freedom as beautiful, natural, and potentially a \"gift from God.\" \"Marvin Gaye released the Let's Get An On album in 1973.\"","year":1973,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 4 - Music of the 70s (Sexual) Revolution","url":null}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":105712887397026,"artist":"Marvin Gaye","artist_id":142830390670993,"title":"Let’s Get It On","year":1973,"ess":1,"yt":"tQj1kPmQXwE","kind":null,"book":{"i